 "edits": [
  {
   "path": "sections.analysis.1.zh",
   "before": "一种解释是，「厚民生」排在「徵兵、轉餉」之前，是把争议最小、也最难被驳倒的目标放在最前面：台谏说的是「鐵路之害」，而避敌、避坟庐这两条或许是对着「害」字去答的（传文未记台谏所指何害）。作者推断这种写法出于策略考虑，传文没有写他的思考过程，此处是作者的解释。",
   "after": "一种解释是，「厚民生」排在「徵兵、轉餉」之前，是把争议最小、也最难被驳倒的目标放在最前面：台谏说的是「鐵路之害」，而不至引敌、坟庐易避这两条或许是对着「害」字去答的（传文未记台谏所指何害）。作者推断这种写法出于策略考虑，传文没有写他的思考过程，此处是作者的解释。",
   "issues": [
    "F1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "path": "sections.analysis.1.en",
   "before": "One reading: putting \"enriching livelihoods\" before \"raising troops and forwarding supplies\" sets the least contested, hardest-to-topple goal at the front. The censors spoke of \"the harms of railways,\" and the two points about avoiding the enemy and sparing graves and houses may answer the word \"harms,\" though the biography does not record which harms were meant. The author infers that this drafting is tactical; the biography records no thought process, so this is the author's interpretation.",
   "after": "One reading: putting \"enriching livelihoods\" before \"raising troops and forwarding supplies\" sets the least contested, hardest-to-topple goal at the front. The censors spoke of \"the harms of railways,\" and the two points about not drawing in the enemy and easily avoiding graves and houses may answer the word \"harms,\" though the biography does not record which harms were meant. The author infers that this drafting is tactical; the biography records no thought process, so this is the author's interpretation.",
   "issues": [
    "F1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "path": "sections.today.0.zh",
   "before": "写一份提案或评审材料时，可以借用这份议奏的顺序：开头不急着罗列优劣，而是先把目标的优先级公开排出来——哪个目标最大、哪个次之，白纸黑字放在最前面；然后把理由写成可以逐条检验的清单，像那六条编号的“利”一样，每条都能被追问“成不成立”。",
   "after": "写一份提案或评审材料时，可以借用这份议奏的顺序：开头不急着罗列优劣，先交代哪个目标最重、哪个其次，把轻重写在最前面；随后把支持的理由分条编号，像那六条编号的“利”一样，每一条都留给读者去追问“成不成立”。",
   "issues": [
    "C1-6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "path": "sections.today.0.en",
   "before": "When drafting a proposal or a review document, you can borrow this memorial's order: rather than opening with a list of pros and cons, first publish the ranking of goals - which goal is greatest, which next, in black and white at the front - and then write the case as a checklist testable point by point, like those six numbered benefits, each open to the challenge: \"does this hold?\"",
   "after": "When drafting a proposal or a review document, you can borrow this memorial's order: rather than opening with a list of pros and cons, state up front which goal weighs most and which comes next; then number the supporting reasons one by one, like those six numbered benefits, leaving each open to the reader's challenge: \"does this hold?\"",
   "issues": [
    "C1-6"
   ]
  }
 ],
